{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Fundamentals","generated":true,"anchor":"Fundamentals","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/NumbersDataAndBasicValues","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/StringsAndText","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Collections","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DatesAndTimes","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FiltersAndSorting"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FoundationEssentials defines the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol to establish conventions for formatting a given type as some kind of output type, typically a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Similarly, the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol provides an API for converting a representation back to the represented type, such as converting a numeric string to an "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Decimal","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While FoundationEssentials defines the core protocols, most implementations of "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseStrategy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" exist in the "},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" module."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" also extends types in both "},{"code":"FoundationEssentials","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the Swift Standard Library to add formatting and parsing support."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When you import ","type":"text"},{"code":"FoundationInternationalization","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", you have two general approaches to perform formatting of supported types:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatted()"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"formatted(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on an instance of the type, optionally passing in a customized "},{"code":"FormatStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" appropriate to the type. These methods, defined by extensions in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FoundationInternationalization"},{"type":"text","text":", are useful for performing one-off formatting with default styles or slightly-customized styles. For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var string123 = Double(1.23).formatted()"},{"type":"text","text":" creates the string "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.23"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"format(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" on an instance of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":", passing in the type you want to format. This method, defined by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" itself, makes sense when you customize a style and want to format many instances with it. For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var string456 = FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>().format(4.56)"},{"type":"text","text":" creates the string "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4.56"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The arrangement is similar with parsing:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(strategy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(_:format:lenient:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to create instance of a type from its formatted representation. For example, to create a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":" from the string "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.23"},{"type":"text","text":", you could use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var oneTwoThree = try Double(\"1.23\", format: FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>())"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"code":"parse(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on an instance of the "},{"code":"ParseStrategy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to initialize an instance of the output type. For example, ","type":"text"},{"code":"var fourFiveSix = try FloatingPointFormatStyle<Double>().parseStrategy.parse(\"4.56\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" creates a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" equal to "},{"code":"4.56","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Data formatting","anchor":"Data-formatting","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseableFormatStyl